--- body ---
## Context
The crash is misdiagnosed. The original ticket says evaluate.py needs a
try/except. Wrong layer.

The real defect: reconcile.py:plants_to_dataframe already detects empty
input (line 47: `if df.empty`) but then ignores its own check and calls
cleaner.clean_dataframe on the empty DataFrame. The cleaner raises
ValueError("The input DataFrame is empty.") — a validation that made
sense when cleaner.py was a standalone stdin tool, but is hostile inside
a pipeline where empty is a valid intermediate state.

Meanwhile, the LP matcher (matching/lp.py:140-150) already handles empty
DataFrames gracefully, producing correct "Only in file1" entries. The
crash sits between two components that would compose correctly without it.

12 empty CSVs exist today (census/gpt-5-mini-run{1,2,3},
census/gpt-5-nano-run{1,2,3}, census/grok-4.20-run3, etc.). These are
not errors — they are valid extraction outcomes where the model produced
a response but no data rows survived extraction. They should produce
measurement records with status="empty" and real zero-metrics (n_plants=0,
tp=0, fp=0, fn=N_ref, f1=0.0) because those are data points that belong
in Pareto charts and method comparisons. A model that extracts zero
plants is worse than one that extracts 80% — but only if both appear in
the measurements table.

The -k flag in experiments/Makefile:177 is the current workaround. It
masks all make errors, not just this one, hiding real build failures.

## Actions
1. In reconcile.py:plants_to_dataframe, return early when the input plant
   list is empty — return a DataFrame with the correct cleaned columns
   (name_clean, province_clean, fuel_clean, capacity_clean, status_clean)
   but zero rows. Do NOT call cleaner.clean_dataframe on empty input.
   This fixes reconcile for all callers: evaluate.py, self_consistency.py,
   query_verification.py.

2. In evaluate.py:_evaluate_csv_file, detect len(system) == 0 after
   load_plants_csv. Still call reconcile (it will now work — producing
   N reference-only entries). Build the RunRecord normally via
   _metrics_to_runrecord, but post-hoc set result_summary.status="empty".
   The metrics (f1=0, fn=N_ref, tp=0, fp=0) compute correctly from the
   all-reference-only reconciliation — no special-casing needed.

3. Remove the -k flag from experiments/Makefile:177. Replace with plain
   -j$(nproc). The -k flag was added by ticket 0036 as a workaround;
   with the crash fixed, it masks real failures.

4. Do NOT touch cleaner.validate_dataframe. That is a separate concern
   (the validation is legacy but removing it risks regressions in other
   callers, and the conference is April 11).

## Test
1. Unit test: reconcile(reference_plants, []) returns len(reference)
   ReconciliationEntry objects, all with match_type=REFERENCE_ONLY.
   No exception raised.

2. Unit test: _evaluate_csv_file on a header-only CSV tmp file produces
   a .record.json with status="empty", f1=0.0, fn=len(reference).

3. Integration: `make -C experiments rebuild-measurements` completes
   without -k flag and without errors. All 12 empty CSVs produce
   .record.json files.

## Exit criteria
- plants_to_dataframe([]) returns empty cleaned DataFrame (no crash)
- Empty CSVs produce status="empty" records with real zero-metrics
- -k flag removed from Makefile evaluate-all-records target
- rebuild-measurements completes cleanly
